  "data_quality_notes": "I unpivoted annual columns using UNION ALL and calculated the % of days in the Very Poor + Severe categories. NULLs or zero totals were handled with COALESCE(...,0) and NULLIF to avoid division-by-zero; as a result, a NULL pct_dangerous (e.g., Surat 2022) indicates missing or zero total-day counts for that city-year. The source table has an inconsistent column name (2023_no_of_days_good1) used for a 'good' count in the 2024 group — this was mapped explicitly; small percentage changes should be interpreted with caution due to those schema quirks and sparse counts for some cities."
